/-!
# P4-Q2-IS: original Wilson depth-one anchor pivot for the physical source obstruction

At the first genuinely higher right-Krylov depth r=1, use HY's NONZERO
zero-mode original two-interacting-Wilson-posterior GI expectation gap as
an anchor. For a genuine physical link/pair boundary (e,z), let d0,d1
be the ORIGINAL GI expectation gaps of the actual depth-zero/one source
modes. The coefficient pivot (-d1,d0) is annihilated by that one anchor.

Finite-dimensional real linear algebra proves this pivot spans the
entire kernel of that original Wilson scalar GI evaluation. Therefore
the genuine physical source separation ker S=ker Phi holds EXACTLY iff:
  (i) the literal physical Haar-L² source S(pivot) vanishes, OR
  (ii) the SAME nonzero coefficient pivot is visible at another original
       interacting-Wilson GI context (Phi(pivot) != 0).

This is a direct test of the first positive-fine-coupling, higher-depth
case using true transfer modes and true posterior expectation gaps.
No assertion that either alternative always holds at positive fine beta.
No independent-Haar conditional, synthetic source frame, Dobrushin
assumption, uniform-in-volume estimate, H1-C3 or continuum mass gap.
-/

